SoundTouchJS AudioWorklet — MPL-2.0  (version 2.1.1, PINNED)
  https://github.com/cutterbl/SoundTouchJS
  Copyright (c) Olli Parviainen, Ryan Berdeen, Jakub Fiala,
  Steve 'Cutter' Blades.
  Underlying SoundTouch library (C++) by Olli Parviainen.
  Vendored unmodified as vendor/soundtouch-processor.js.
  Licence text: vendor/LICENSE.soundtouch-processor.txt.

  UPGRADED 2026-08-18, from 0.3.0 (LGPL-2.1) to 2.1.1 (MPL-2.0). The reason
  was a defect, not housekeeping. 0.3.0's process() pushed 128 frames into the
  stretcher and assumed 128 came back, writing the untouched remainder of a
  zero-filled array to the output whenever fewer were ready — and its
  receiveSamples() returns undefined, so it could not detect this. Measured
  offline against the vendored bytes: 0 gaps/sec unstretched, 10 gaps/sec and
  7.3% silent output frames at tempo 1.08. 2.1.1 doing the equivalent work
  measured 0 gaps/sec.

  The obligation in force is therefore MPL-2.0. Both are file-level copyleft
  and the file is vendored unmodified, so the practical requirement is
  unchanged: ship the licence text and say where the source came from.

  vendor/soundtouch-worklet.js (0.3.0, LGPL-2.1) and its licence text are
  RETAINED ON DISK so the two can be A/B'd by ear. Nothing loads it. If 2.1.1
  is kept, the retained 0.3.0 file and its LGPL text stay in vendor/ by
  decision (2026-09-01): they are what the upgrade replaced and the table
  documents them as NOT loaded. The obligation in force is MPL-2.0. The LGPL-2.1
  obligation travels with the distribution for a file the app never uses.

  HISTORICAL CORRECTION, 2026-08-17, kept because the failure is instructive.
  This entry once read "MPL-2.0 (current versions)" while the application
  actually loaded 0.3.0 under LGPL-2.1: deckwave.js requested an UNPINNED
  jsdelivr URL, and the 2.x releases do not contain that path — the directory
  is ".dist", with a leading dot — so the request silently resolved to 0.3.0.
  Verified at the time by sha256. Pin your version: an unpinned dependency can
  change your obligations, and here it already had.

