INFLUENCES (no code used or copied)
-----------------------------------
Strudel — strudel.cc, codeberg.org/uzu/strudel
  Felix Roos, Alex McLean and contributors. The visual vocabulary here
  (scope, spectrum, punchcard, pitchwheel) follows Strudel's built-in
  feedback set. These are independent implementations on the Web Audio
  AnalyserNode.

CRAWNiiK / browser-visualizer-v1 (MIT) — https://github.com/CRAWNiiK
  Assessed 2026-08-21 as prior art and found unrelated in provenance. Listed
  here because the assessment is not the whole story: the projector-window
  idea in `⇱ popout` came from looking at that project. No code was used or
  copied; the idea was.


TidalCycles — Alex McLean. Strudel's ancestor.

Switch Angel — whose Strudel live-coding work is where these visuals were
  first pointed out to the author.

Winamp / AVS / Milkdrop — the general debt for what a music player looks
  like. No Winamp code, assets, skins or audio are used. Note that Winamp's
  2024 source release is under a restrictive licence and is NOT used here.
  (Since 2026-08-21 the Milkdrop LINEAGE does ship via butterchurn — see
  its entry above — which descends from the 2013 BSD release, not from the
  2024 one.)

STANDARDS
---------
VU meter ballistics follow ANSI C16.5-1942, now incorporated into
IEC 60268-17: full-wave averaging reaching 99% deflection in 300ms.
